  "Question": "If the parabola \\(y=ax^2+bx+c\\) passes through the points \\((-1,12),\\) \\((0,5),\\) and \\((2,-3),\\) the value of \\(a+b+c\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-4\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The point with \\(x=0\\) is the easiest starting point because it immediately gives \\(c=5\\). Substituting the other two points then gives\n\\[\na-b+5=12,\\qquad 4a+2b+5=-3.\n\\]\nAfter simplifying, these become\n\\[\na-b=7,\\qquad 2a+b=-4.\n\\]\nAdding the equations eliminates \\(b\\), leaving \\(3a=3\\), so \\(a=1\\). The first equation now gives \\(b=-6\\). Therefore\n\\[\na+b+c=1-6+5=\\boxed{0},\n\\]\nwhich is choice C.",
